    "extraction_notes": [
      "PDF SHA-256 verified as 00cf4e28a7fc077c84d01ab1e69ee642192e5b72ed40534e80593cc1f6faefcb.",
      "Identity verified: the supplied PDF visibly identifies S9013-E, MDD/Microdiode branding, an NPN transistor, SOT-23 package, and Rev:2024A1.",
      "The supplied PDF has five pages; electrical characteristics and typical-characteristics plots are on p. 1 and p. 2. All five pages were examined.",
      "Electrical characteristics are specified at TA = 25 degC unless otherwise specified. The hFE table gives a minimum of 120 and maximum of 400 at IC = 50 mA and VCE = 1 V; the classification table gives rank ranges L = 120-200, H = 200-350, and J = 300-400, but no rank was inferred for this exact part.",
      "Maximum ratings include VCBO = 40 V, VCEO = 25 V, VEBO = 5 V, continuous IC = 0.5 A, PC = 0.3 W, Tj = 150 degC, and Tstg = -55 to +150 degC at TA = 25 degC unless otherwise noted.",
      "VCE(sat) and VBE(sat) table values are guaranteed maximums, not typical values. The p. 2 beta = 10 curves were digitized separately as typical visual read-offs and were not substituted for the guaranteed table bounds.",
      "The p. 2 hFE, VCE(sat), VBE(sat), capacitance, and fT curves were manually digitized at visible axis positions. Values are direct plot read-offs in SI units; no interpolation was used.",
      "Cobo is tabulated only as a maximum of 8 pF at VCB = 6 V, IE = 0, f = 1 MHz. Cibo is not tabulated; its value is represented only by a digitized typical Cib curve point at VEB = 1 V.",
      "The p. 2 capacitance plot states f = 1 MHz, IE = 0 / IC = 0, TA = 25 degC. The p. 2 fT plot states VCE = 6 V and TA = 25 degC; the p. 1 fT specification is a guaranteed minimum at IC = 20 mA with measurement frequency f = 30 MHz."
